+/*
+ * The external QCA8337 is driven by qca-ssdk as a second ESS device
+ * (device_id 1, which registers as swconfig "switch1"), the same way the
+ * vendor/NSS stack does it.
+ *
+ * It is deliberately NOT described as a mainline DSA switch: DSA inserts a
+ * 2-byte QCA tag at offset 12 of every frame on the CPU link.  The NSS
+ * firmware then reads 0x80xx as the ethertype, fails to parse L3 and
+ * exceptions 100% of the traffic to the host CPU (eth_rx_unknown_l3_protocol),
+ * and ECM cannot build an interface hierarchy over DSA user ports.  DSA also
+ * binds a single conduit, which left GMAC0/eth0 unused and forced LAN+WAN
+ * through eth1 alone - that is the "WAN cannot work if added" note that used
+ * to sit on port@5 here.
